IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `ccc-core`

-- ccc28-part25-forfeiture.l4 -- Criminal Code (Canada), sections 762 to 773 (PART XXV, Effect and Enforcement of Undertakings, Release Orders and Recognizances):
-- where applications for forfeiture are made, the continuing force of the documents, the render of an accused by sureties, substitution of a surety, the endorsement of a default,
-- proceedings on a default, the levy under a writ of fieri facias, and committal when a writ is not satisfied. Layer 1 of part ccc28.
-- Source: a plain-text rendering, made by a converter script, of the Justice Laws Website consolidation (current to 2026-09-30); it is not the official text, and nothing here is
-- claimed verified against the official text. The Schedule to this Part (columns I, II and III) is in another part's range: its answers are inputs here (seam, NOTES.md).
-- READING A RESULT: JUST FALSE where the text says no in its own words (a failed "if" or "where" on a duty, a "no ... shall", a "means", a period it fixes); NOTHING where it is silent or limited
-- by its own wording (a named class, a "without", a named complement, a grant under an "if"); the court's own judgments (suitable, proper, the ends of justice) are inputs.
-- The three documents of this Part are the core's `Process document` constructors `an undertaking`, `a release order` and `a recognizance`.
-- The Code's `Form 27`, `Form 33` and `Form 34` are outside this range: the text of a Form is not encoded here; that a certificate is "in Form 33" is an input.

§ `Helpers (not law)`

-- helper: the document is one of the three named in section 763(1) and in section 770(1): an undertaking, a release order or a recognizance.
GIVEN document IS A `Process document`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 763 the document is an undertaking, a release order or a recognizance` MEANS
    document EQUALS `an undertaking` OR document EQUALS `a release order` OR document EQUALS `a recognizance`

-- helper: the document is one of the two named in section 764(1), 764(4) and 765: an undertaking or a release order.
GIVEN document IS A `Process document`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 764 the document is an undertaking or a release order` MEANS
    document EQUALS `an undertaking` OR document EQUALS `a release order`

-- helper: the document is one of the two named in section 766, 767 and 767.1, which speak of a surety: a release order or a recognizance.
GIVEN document IS A `Process document`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 766 the document is a release order or a recognizance` MEANS
    document EQUALS `a release order` OR document EQUALS `a recognizance`

§ `Part XXV, section 762: where applications for forfeiture are made`

-- (1) "Applications for the forfeiture of an amount set out in an undertaking, release order or recognizance must be made to the courts designated in column II of the schedule of the respective
-- provinces designated in column I of the schedule."  Which court column II designates for a province is the Schedule (another part's range): taken as the fact that the application is made to it.
-- src:16541 | 762 (1) Applications for the forfeiture of an amount set out in an undertaking, release order or recognizance must be made to the courts designated in column II of the schedule of the respective provinces designated in column I of the schedule.
@ref s 762(1) (src:16541)
GIVEN document IS A `Process document`
      `the application is an application for the forfeiture of an amount set out in the document` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the application is made to the court designated in column II of the schedule for the province designated in column I` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 762(1) the application for forfeiture is made to the court the schedule designates` MEANS
    IF NOT (`s 763 the document is an undertaking, a release order or a recognizance` document AND `the application is an application for the forfeiture of an amount set out in the document`)
    THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Applications for the forfeiture of an amount set out in an undertaking, release order or recognizance": the subsection speaks of those applications, and is silent about any other
    ELSE IF `the application is made to the court designated in column II of the schedule for the province designated in column I`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "must be made to the courts designated in column II of the schedule of the respective provinces designated in column I of the schedule"

-- (2) "In this Part, clerk of the court means the officer designated in column III of the schedule in respect of the court designated in column II of the schedule".
-- src:16543 | (2) In this Part,
-- src:16544 | clerk of the court means the officer designated in column III of the schedule in respect of the court designated in column II of the schedule; (greffier du tribunal)
@ref s 762(2) "clerk of the court" (src:16543-16544)
GIVEN `the person is the officer designated in column III of the schedule in respect of the court designated in column II of the schedule` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 762(2) the person is the clerk of the court` MEANS
    IF `the person is the officer designated in column III of the schedule in respect of the court designated in column II of the schedule`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "clerk of the court means the officer designated in column III of the schedule in respect of the court designated in column II of the schedule"

-- "schedule means the schedule to this Part": a pointer to the schedule, which is another part's range.
-- src:16545 | schedule means the schedule to this Part. (annexe)
@ref s 762(2) "schedule" (src:16545)
GIVEN `the document is the schedule to this Part` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 762(2) the document is the schedule` MEANS
    IF `the document is the schedule to this Part`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "schedule means the schedule to this Part"

§ `Part XXV, section 763: the undertaking, release order or recognizance continues to bind`

-- (1) "If a person is bound by an undertaking, release order or recognizance to appear before a court, provincial court judge or justice for any purpose and the session or sittings of that court or the
-- proceedings are adjourned or an order is made changing the place of trial, that person and their sureties continue to be bound by the undertaking, release order or recognizance as if it had been entered
-- into or issued with respect to the resumed proceedings or the trial at the time and place at which the proceedings are ordered to be resumed or the trial is ordered to be held."
-- src:16547 | 763 (1) If a person is bound by an undertaking, release order or recognizance to appear before a court, provincial court judge or justice for any purpose and the session or sittings of that court or the proceedings are adjourned or an order is made changing the place of trial, that person and their sureties continue to be bound by the undertaking, release order or recognizance as if it had been entered into or issued with respect to the resumed proceedings or the trial at the time and place at which the proceedings are ordered to be resumed or the trial is ordered to be held.
@ref s 763(1) (src:16547)
GIVEN document IS A `Process document`
      `the person is bound by the document to appear before a court, provincial court judge or justice for any purpose` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the session or sittings of that court or the proceedings are adjourned` IS A BOOLEAN
      `an order is made changing the place of trial` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 763(1) the person and their sureties continue to be bound` MEANS
    IF NOT (`s 763 the document is an undertaking, a release order or a recognizance` document)
    THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "an undertaking, release order or recognizance": the subsection names three documents, and is silent about any other
    ELSE IF `the person is bound by the document to appear before a court, provincial court judge or justice for any purpose` AND (`the session or sittings of that court or the proceedings are adjourned` OR `an order is made changing the place of trial`)
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If a person is bound by an undertaking, release order or recognizance to appear before a court, provincial court judge or justice for any purpose and the session or sittings of that court or the proceedings are adjourned or an order is made changing the place of trial"

-- (2) "A summary of section 763 must be set out in any undertaking, release order or recognizance."  A bare "must": the document that lacks the summary does not comply (fork F10: JUST FALSE).
-- src:16549 | (2) A summary of section 763 must be set out in any undertaking, release order or recognizance.
@ref s 763(2) (src:16549)
GIVEN document IS A `Process document`
      `a summary of section 763 is set out in the document` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 763(2) the document sets out a summary of section 763 as it must` MEANS
    IF NOT (`s 763 the document is an undertaking, a release order or a recognizance` document)
    THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "any undertaking, release order or recognizance"
    ELSE IF `a summary of section 763 is set out in the document`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A summary of section 763 must be set out in any undertaking, release order or recognizance"

§ `Part XXV, sections 764 and 765: the undertaking or release order binds the accused until discharged or sentenced`

-- (1) "If an accused is bound by an undertaking or release order to appear for trial, their arraignment or conviction does not cancel the undertaking or release order, and it continues to bind them and their sureties
-- for their appearance until the accused is discharged or sentenced, as the case may be."
-- src:16551 | 764 (1) If an accused is bound by an undertaking or release order to appear for trial, their arraignment or conviction does not cancel the undertaking or release order, and it continues to bind them and their sureties for their appearance until the accused is discharged or sentenced, as the case may be.
@ref s 764(1) (src:16551)
GIVEN document IS A `Process document`
      `the accused is bound by the document to appear for trial` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the accused is discharged or sentenced` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 764(1) the undertaking or release order continues to bind the accused and their sureties for their appearance` MEANS
    IF NOT (`s 764 the document is an undertaking or a release order` document)
    THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "an undertaking or release order": a recognizance is not named in this subsection
    ELSE IF NOT `the accused is bound by the document to appear for trial`
         THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If an accused is bound by an undertaking or release order to appear for trial"
         ELSE IF `the accused is discharged or sentenced`
              THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "until the accused is discharged or sentenced, as the case may be"
              ELSE JUST TRUE

-- (2) "Despite subsection (1), the court, provincial court judge or justice may commit an accused to prison or may require them to furnish new or additional sureties for their appearance until the accused is
-- discharged or sentenced, as the case may be."  A power ("may"): the gate is the period "until the accused is discharged or sentenced" (an "until" gate: JUST FALSE, listed in NOTES.md group (i)).
DECLARE `s 764(2) step` IS ONE OF
    `s 764(2) commit the accused to prison`
    `s 764(2) require the accused to furnish new or additional sureties for their appearance`
    `s 764(2) a step the subsection does not name`

-- src:16553 | (2) Despite subsection (1), the court, provincial court judge or justice may commit an accused to prison or may require them to furnish new or additional sureties for their appearance until the accused is discharged or sentenced, as the case may be.
@ref s 764(2) (src:16553)
GIVEN `the accused is bound by an undertaking or release order to appear for trial` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the accused is discharged or sentenced` IS A BOOLEAN
      step IS A `s 764(2) step`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 764(2) the court, provincial court judge or justice may take this step` MEANS
    IF NOT `the accused is bound by an undertaking or release order to appear for trial`
    THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Despite subsection (1)": the power is given against the background of subsection (1), and the subsection is silent about an accused not so bound
    ELSE IF `the accused is discharged or sentenced`
         THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "until the accused is discharged or sentenced, as the case may be"
         ELSE CONSIDER step
              WHEN `s 764(2) commit the accused to prison` THEN JUST TRUE
              WHEN `s 764(2) require the accused to furnish new or additional sureties for their appearance` THEN JUST TRUE
              WHEN `s 764(2) a step the subsection does not name` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): the two steps are not closed with "only"

-- (3) "The sureties of an accused who is bound by a release order to appear for trial are discharged if the accused is committed to prison under subsection (2)."
-- src:16555 | (3) The sureties of an accused who is bound by a release order to appear for trial are discharged if the accused is committed to prison under subsection (2).
@ref s 764(3) (src:16555)
GIVEN document IS A `Process document`
      `the accused is bound by the document to appear for trial` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the accused is committed to prison under subsection (2)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 764(3) the sureties of the accused are discharged` MEANS
    IF NOT (document EQUALS `a release order`)
    THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "an accused who is bound by a release order": an undertaking and a recognizance are not named in this subsection
    ELSE IF `the accused is bound by the document to appear for trial` AND `the accused is committed to prison under subsection (2)`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "are discharged if the accused is committed to prison under subsection (2)"

-- (4) "A summary of subsections (1) to (3) must be set out in any undertaking or release order."  A bare "must": JUST FALSE for a document that lacks the summary (fork F10).
-- src:16557 | (4) A summary of subsections (1) to (3) must be set out in any undertaking or release order.
@ref s 764(4) (src:16557)
GIVEN document IS A `Process document`
      `a summary of subsections (1) to (3) is set out in the document` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 764(4) the document sets out a summary of subsections (1) to (3) as it must` MEANS
    IF NOT (`s 764 the document is an undertaking or a release order` document)
    THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "any undertaking or release order": a recognizance is not named in this subsection
    ELSE IF `a summary of subsections (1) to (3) is set out in the document`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A summary of subsections (1) to (3) must be set out in any undertaking or release order"

-- 765 "If an accused is bound by an undertaking or a release order to appear for trial, their arrest on another charge does not cancel the undertaking or release order, and it continues to bind them and their
-- sureties for their appearance until the accused is discharged or sentenced, as the case may be, in respect of the offence to which the undertaking or release order relates."
-- src:16559 | 765 If an accused is bound by an undertaking or a release order to appear for trial, their arrest on another charge does not cancel the undertaking or release order, and it continues to bind them and their sureties for their appearance until the accused is discharged or sentenced, as the case may be, in respect of the offence to which the undertaking or release order relates.
@ref s 765 (src:16559)
GIVEN document IS A `Process document`
      `the accused is bound by the document to appear for trial` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the accused is discharged or sentenced in respect of the offence to which the document relates` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 765 the undertaking or release order continues to bind the accused and their sureties despite the arrest on another charge` MEANS
    IF NOT (`s 764 the document is an undertaking or a release order` document)
    THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "an undertaking or a release order": a recognizance is not named in this section
    ELSE IF NOT `the accused is bound by the document to appear for trial`
         THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If an accused is bound by an undertaking or a release order to appear for trial"
         ELSE IF `the accused is discharged or sentenced in respect of the offence to which the document relates`
              THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "until the accused is discharged or sentenced, as the case may be, in respect of the offence to which the undertaking or release order relates"
              ELSE JUST TRUE

§ `Part XXV, sections 766 to 769: render of the accused by sureties`

-- 766(1) "A surety for a person who is subject to a release order or recognizance may, by an application in writing to a court, provincial court judge or justice, apply to be relieved of their obligation under the release
-- order or recognizance, and the court, provincial court judge or justice shall then make an order in writing for committal of that person to the prison named in that order."
-- An undertaking has no surety, and the subsection names a release order and a recognizance: a case outside them is not covered.
-- src:16561 | 766 (1) A surety for a person who is subject to a release order or recognizance may, by an application in writing to a court, provincial court judge or justice, apply to be relieved of their obligation under the release order or recognizance, and the court, provincial court judge or justice shall then make an order in writing for committal of that person to the prison named in that order.
@ref s 766(1) (src:16561)
GIVEN document IS A `Process document`
      `the surety applies in writing to a court, provincial court judge or justice` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 766(1) the surety may apply to be relieved of their obligation` MEANS
    IF NOT (`s 766 the document is a release order or a recognizance` document)
    THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "a person who is subject to a release order or recognizance": an undertaking is not named in this subsection
    ELSE IF `the surety applies in writing to a court, provincial court judge or justice`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "by an application in writing to a court, provincial court judge or justice": the subsection names this way of applying, and does not say that no other way is open

-- src:16561 | 766 (1) A surety for a person who is subject to a release order or recognizance may, by an application in writing to a court, provincial court judge or justice, apply to be relieved of their obligation under the release order or recognizance, and the court, provincial court judge or justice shall then make an order in writing for committal of that person to the prison named in that order.
@ref s 766(1) (src:16561)
GIVEN document IS A `Process document`
      `the surety has applied in writing to be relieved of their obligation under subsection (1)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 766(1) the court, provincial court judge or justice shall make an order in writing for committal of the person` MEANS
    IF NOT (`s 766 the document is a release order or a recognizance` document)
    THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "a release order or recognizance"
    ELSE IF `the surety has applied in writing to be relieved of their obligation under subsection (1)`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "shall then make an order in writing for committal of that person"

DECLARE `s 766(1) action` IS ONE OF
    `s 766(1) make an order in writing for committal of the person to the prison named in the order`

-- src:16561 | 766 (1) A surety for a person who is subject to a release order or recognizance may, by an application in writing to a court, provincial court judge or justice, apply to be relieved of their obligation under the release order or recognizance, and the court, provincial court judge or justice shall then make an order in writing for committal of that person to the prison named in that order.
@ref s 766(1) (src:16561)
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 766(1) action`
`s 766(1) the court's duty to commit the person on the surety's application` MEANS
    PARTY `the court`
    MUST `s 766(1) make an order in writing for committal of the person to the prison named in the order`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY `the court` BECAUSE "the court did not make an order in writing for committal of the person on the surety's application"

-- (2) "An order issued by a court, provincial court judge or justice under subsection (1) must be given to the surety and, on receipt of it, the surety or any peace officer may arrest the person named in the order and
-- deliver that person with the order to the keeper of the prison named in the order, and the keeper shall receive and imprison that person until the person is discharged according to law."
-- The text does not say who gives the order to the surety (fork F11): the function asks only whether it has been given.
-- src:16563 | (2) An order issued by a court, provincial court judge or justice under subsection (1) must be given to the surety and, on receipt of it, the surety or any peace officer may arrest the person named in the order and deliver that person with the order to the keeper of the prison named in the order, and the keeper shall receive and imprison that person until the person is discharged according to law.
@ref s 766(2) (src:16563)
GIVEN `the order is issued under subsection (1)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the order has been given to the surety` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 766(2) the order is given to the surety as it must be` MEANS
    IF NOT `the order is issued under subsection (1)`
    THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "An order issued by a court, provincial court judge or justice under subsection (1)"
    ELSE IF `the order has been given to the surety`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "must be given to the surety"

DECLARE `s 766(2) arrester` IS ONE OF
    `s 766(2) the surety`
    `s 766(2) a peace officer`
    `s 766(2) another person`

GIVEN arrester IS A `s 766(2) arrester`
      `the surety or peace officer has received the order` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 766(2) this person may arrest the person named in the order and deliver them to the keeper of the prison` MEANS
    IF NOT `the surety or peace officer has received the order`
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "on receipt of it"
    ELSE CONSIDER arrester
         WHEN `s 766(2) the surety` THEN JUST TRUE
         WHEN `s 766(2) a peace officer` THEN JUST TRUE
         WHEN `s 766(2) another person` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "the surety or any peace officer": the subsection names who may arrest, and does not say that no one else may

GIVEN `the person is delivered with the order to the keeper of the prison named in the order` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person has been discharged according to law` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 766(2) the keeper shall receive and imprison the person` MEANS
    IF NOT `the person is delivered with the order to the keeper of the prison named in the order`
    THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "deliver that person with the order to the keeper of the prison named in the order": the keeper's duty is stated for a person so delivered
    ELSE IF `the person has been discharged according to law`
         THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "until the person is discharged according to law"
         ELSE JUST TRUE

DECLARE `s 766(2) action` IS ONE OF
    `s 766(2) receive and imprison the person`

-- src:16563 | (2) An order issued by a court, provincial court judge or justice under subsection (1) must be given to the surety and, on receipt of it, the surety or any peace officer may arrest the person named in the order and deliver that person with the order to the keeper of the prison named in the order, and the keeper shall receive and imprison that person until the person is discharged according to law.
@ref s 766(2) (src:16563)
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 766(2) action`
`s 766(2) the keeper's duty to receive and imprison the person` MEANS
    PARTY `the keeper of a prison`
    MUST `s 766(2) receive and imprison the person`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY `the keeper of a prison` BECAUSE "the keeper of the prison did not receive and imprison the person delivered with the order"

-- (3) "If a court, provincial court judge or justice issues an order under subsection (1) and receives from the sheriff a certificate that the person named in the order has been committed to prison under subsection (2),
-- the court, provincial court judge or justice shall order an entry of the committal to be endorsed on the release order or recognizance, as the case may be."
-- The text speaks of a certificate from "the sheriff", yet subsection (2) names the keeper of the prison and no sheriff (numbered finding in NOTES.md).
-- src:16565 | (3) If a court, provincial court judge or justice issues an order under subsection (1) and receives from the sheriff a certificate that the person named in the order has been committed to prison under subsection (2), the court, provincial court judge or justice shall order an entry of the committal to be endorsed on the release order or recognizance, as the case may be.
@ref s 766(3) (src:16565)
GIVEN document IS A `Process document`
      `the court, provincial court judge or justice issues an order under subsection (1)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the court, provincial court judge or justice receives from the sheriff a certificate that the person named in the order has been committed to prison under subsection (2)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 766(3) the court, provincial court judge or justice shall order an entry of the committal to be endorsed on the document` MEANS
    IF NOT (`s 766 the document is a release order or a recognizance` document)
    THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "the release order or recognizance, as the case may be"
    ELSE IF `the court, provincial court judge or justice issues an order under subsection (1)` AND `the court, provincial court judge or justice receives from the sheriff a certificate that the person named in the order has been committed to prison under subsection (2)`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If a court, provincial court judge or justice issues an order under subsection (1) and receives from the sheriff a certificate"

DECLARE `s 766(3) action` IS ONE OF
    `s 766(3) order an entry of the committal to be endorsed on the release order or recognizance`

-- src:16565 | (3) If a court, provincial court judge or justice issues an order under subsection (1) and receives from the sheriff a certificate that the person named in the order has been committed to prison under subsection (2), the court, provincial court judge or justice shall order an entry of the committal to be endorsed on the release order or recognizance, as the case may be.
@ref s 766(3) (src:16565)
