-- (4) "An endorsement under subsection (3) cancels the release order or recognizance, as the case may be, and discharges the sureties."
-- src:16567 | (4) An endorsement under subsection (3) cancels the release order or recognizance, as the case may be, and discharges the sureties.
@ref s 766(4) (src:16567)
GIVEN `an endorsement is made under subsection (3)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 766(4) the release order or recognizance is cancelled and the sureties are discharged` MEANS
    IF `an endorsement is made under subsection (3)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "An endorsement under subsection (3) cancels": the subsection speaks of that endorsement, and is silent about any other way the document is cancelled

-- 767 "A surety for a person who is subject to a release order or recognizance may bring that person before the court where the person is required to appear or where the person entered into the recognizance at any time
-- during the sittings of that court and before the person's trial, and the surety may discharge their obligation under the release order or recognizance by giving that person into the custody of the court. The court
-- shall then commit that person to prison until the person is discharged according to law."
DECLARE `s 767 place` IS ONE OF
    `s 767 the court where the person is required to appear`
    `s 767 the court where the person entered into the recognizance`
    `s 767 another court`

-- src:16569 | 767 A surety for a person who is subject to a release order or recognizance may bring that person before the court where the person is required to appear or where the person entered into the recognizance at any time during the sittings of that court and before the person’s trial, and the surety may discharge their obligation under the release order or recognizance by giving that person into the custody of the court. The court shall then commit that person to prison until the person is discharged according to law.
@ref s 767 (src:16569)
GIVEN document IS A `Process document`
      place IS A `s 767 place`
      `it is during the sittings of that court` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is before the person's trial` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 767 the surety may bring the person before the court` MEANS
    IF NOT (`s 766 the document is a release order or a recognizance` document)
    THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "a release order or recognizance"
    ELSE IF NOT (`it is during the sittings of that court` AND `it is before the person's trial`)
         THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "at any time during the sittings of that court and before the person's trial"
         ELSE CONSIDER place
              WHEN `s 767 the court where the person is required to appear` THEN JUST TRUE
              WHEN `s 767 the court where the person entered into the recognizance` THEN JUST TRUE
              WHEN `s 767 another court` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "the court where the person is required to appear or where the person entered into the recognizance": the section names the courts, and does not say that no other court will do

-- src:16569 | 767 A surety for a person who is subject to a release order or recognizance may bring that person before the court where the person is required to appear or where the person entered into the recognizance at any time during the sittings of that court and before the person’s trial, and the surety may discharge their obligation under the release order or recognizance by giving that person into the custody of the court. The court shall then commit that person to prison until the person is discharged according to law.
@ref s 767 (src:16569)
GIVEN `the surety gives the person into the custody of the court` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 767 the surety discharges their obligation under the release order or recognizance` MEANS
    IF `the surety gives the person into the custody of the court`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "by giving that person into the custody of the court": the section names this way of discharging the obligation, and does not say that no other way does

-- src:16569 | 767 A surety for a person who is subject to a release order or recognizance may bring that person before the court where the person is required to appear or where the person entered into the recognizance at any time during the sittings of that court and before the person’s trial, and the surety may discharge their obligation under the release order or recognizance by giving that person into the custody of the court. The court shall then commit that person to prison until the person is discharged according to law.
@ref s 767 (src:16569)
GIVEN `the surety has given the person into the custody of the court` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person has been discharged according to law` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 767 the court shall commit the person to prison` MEANS
    IF NOT `the surety has given the person into the custody of the court`
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The court shall then commit that person to prison"
    ELSE IF `the person has been discharged according to law`
         THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "until the person is discharged according to law"
         ELSE JUST TRUE

DECLARE `s 767 action` IS ONE OF
    `s 767 commit the person to prison`

-- src:16569 | 767 A surety for a person who is subject to a release order or recognizance may bring that person before the court where the person is required to appear or where the person entered into the recognizance at any time during the sittings of that court and before the person’s trial, and the surety may discharge their obligation under the release order or recognizance by giving that person into the custody of the court. The court shall then commit that person to prison until the person is discharged according to law.
@ref s 767 (src:16569)
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 767 action`
`s 767 the court's duty to commit the person to prison` MEANS
    PARTY `the court`
    MUST `s 767 commit the person to prison`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY `the court` BECAUSE "the court did not commit the person to prison after the surety gave them into the custody of the court"

-- 767.1(1) "If a surety for a person who is subject to a release order or recognizance has given the person into the custody of a court under section 767, or a surety applies to be relieved of their obligation under the
-- release order or recognizance under subsection 766(1), the court, justice or provincial court judge, as the case may be, may, instead of committing or issuing an order for the committal of the person to prison,
-- substitute any other suitable person for the surety under the release order or recognizance."  A power ("may") under an "if" gate: NOTHING when the gate fails (fork F3).
-- src:16571 | 767.1 (1) If a surety for a person who is subject to a release order or recognizance has given the person into the custody of a court under section 767, or a surety applies to be relieved of their obligation under the release order or recognizance under subsection 766(1), the court, justice or provincial court judge, as the case may be, may, instead of committing or issuing an order for the committal of the person to prison, substitute any other suitable person for the surety under the release order or recognizance.
-- src:16572 | Signing of release order or recognizance by new sureties
@ref s 767.1(1) (src:16571-16572)
GIVEN `the surety has given the person into the custody of a court under section 767` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the surety applies to be relieved of their obligation under subsection 766(1)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the other person is suitable, in the opinion of the court, justice or provincial court judge` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 767.1(1) the court, justice or provincial court judge may substitute another person for the surety` MEANS
    IF NOT (`the surety has given the person into the custody of a court under section 767` OR `the surety applies to be relieved of their obligation under subsection 766(1)`)
    THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "If a surety ... has given the person into the custody of a court under section 767, or a surety applies to be relieved of their obligation": a grant limited by an "if" gate; the subsection does not say the court may not substitute a person otherwise
    ELSE IF `the other person is suitable, in the opinion of the court, justice or provincial court judge`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "any other suitable person": the power is to substitute a suitable person, and the subsection is silent about an unsuitable one

-- (2) "If a person substituted for a surety under a release order or recognizance under subsection (1) signs the release order or recognizance, the original surety is discharged, but the release order or
-- recognizance is not otherwise affected."
-- src:16573 | (2) If a person substituted for a surety under a release order or recognizance under subsection (1) signs the release order or recognizance, the original surety is discharged, but the release order or recognizance is not otherwise affected.
@ref s 767.1(2) (src:16573)
GIVEN `a person is substituted for a surety under subsection (1)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the substituted person signs the release order or recognizance` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 767.1(2) the original surety is discharged` MEANS
    IF `a person is substituted for a surety under subsection (1)` AND `the substituted person signs the release order or recognizance`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If a person substituted for a surety under a release order or recognizance under subsection (1) signs the release order or recognizance, the original surety is discharged"

-- 768 "Nothing in this Part limits any right that a surety has of taking and giving into custody any person for whom they are a surety under a release order or recognizance."  A flat negative.
-- src:16575 | 768 Nothing in this Part limits any right that a surety has of taking and giving into custody any person for whom they are a surety under a release order or recognizance.
@ref s 768 (src:16575)
GIVEN `the right is a right that a surety has of taking and giving into custody a person for whom they are a surety under a release order or recognizance` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 768 this Part limits the surety's right of taking and giving the person into custody` MEANS
    IF `the right is a right that a surety has of taking and giving into custody a person for whom they are a surety under a release order or recognizance`
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Nothing in this Part limits any right that a surety has of taking and giving into custody any person"
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "any right that a surety has of taking and giving into custody": the section is silent about any other right

-- 769 "Where a surety for a person has rendered him into custody and that person has been committed to prison, the provisions of Parts XVI, XXI and XXVII relating to judicial interim release apply, with such
-- modifications as the circumstances require, in respect of him and he shall forthwith be taken before a justice or judge as an accused charged with an offence or as an appellant, as the case may be, for the purposes of those provisions."
-- src:16577 | 769 Where a surety for a person has rendered him into custody and that person has been committed to prison, the provisions of Parts XVI, XXI and XXVII relating to judicial interim release apply, with such modifications as the circumstances require, in respect of him and he shall forthwith be taken before a justice or judge as an accused charged with an offence or as an appellant, as the case may be, for the purposes of those provisions.
@ref s 769 (src:16577)
GIVEN `a surety for the person has rendered the person into custody` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person has been committed to prison` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 769 the interim release provisions of Parts XVI, XXI and XXVII apply in respect of the person` MEANS
    IF `a surety for the person has rendered the person into custody` AND `the person has been committed to prison`
    THEN JUST TRUE   -- with such modifications as the circumstances require: the modifications are in Parts XVI, XXI and XXVII, outside this range
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where a surety for a person has rendered him into custody and that person has been committed to prison"

GIVEN `a surety for the person has rendered the person into custody` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person has been committed to prison` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 769 the person shall forthwith be taken before a justice or judge` MEANS
    IF `a surety for the person has rendered the person into custody` AND `the person has been committed to prison`
    THEN JUST TRUE   -- as an accused charged with an offence or as an appellant, as the case may be: "forthwith" is not given as a number of hours
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where a surety for a person has rendered him into custody and that person has been committed to prison"

§ `Part XXV, section 770: default to be endorsed`

-- (1) "If, in proceedings to which this Act applies, a person who is subject to an undertaking, release order or recognizance does not comply with any of its conditions, a court, provincial court judge or justice
-- having knowledge of the facts shall endorse or cause to be endorsed on the undertaking, release order or recognizance a certificate in Form 33 setting out (a) the nature of the default; (b) the reason for the
-- default, if it is known; (c) whether the ends of justice have been defeated or delayed by reason of the default; and (d) the names and addresses of the principal and sureties."
-- src:16579 | 770 (1) If, in proceedings to which this Act applies, a person who is subject to an undertaking, release order or recognizance does not comply with any of its conditions, a court, provincial court judge or justice having knowledge of the facts shall endorse or cause to be endorsed on the undertaking, release order or recognizance a certificate in Form 33 setting out
@ref s 770(1) (src:16579)
GIVEN document IS A `Process document`
      `the proceedings are proceedings to which this Act applies` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person subject to the document does not comply with any of its conditions` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the court, provincial court judge or justice has knowledge of the facts` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 770(1) the court, provincial court judge or justice shall endorse or cause to be endorsed a certificate` MEANS
    IF NOT (`s 763 the document is an undertaking, a release order or a recognizance` document)
    THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "an undertaking, release order or recognizance"
    ELSE IF     `the proceedings are proceedings to which this Act applies`
            AND `the person subject to the document does not comply with any of its conditions`
            AND `the court, provincial court judge or justice has knowledge of the facts`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If, in proceedings to which this Act applies, a person who is subject to an undertaking, release order or recognizance does not comply with any of its conditions, a court, provincial court judge or justice having knowledge of the facts shall endorse"

-- src:16580 | (a) the nature of the default;
-- src:16581 | (b) the reason for the default, if it is known;
-- src:16582 | (c) whether the ends of justice have been defeated or delayed by reason of the default; and
-- src:16583 | (d) the names and addresses of the principal and sureties.
@ref s 770(1) (a) to (d) (src:16580-16583)
GIVEN `the certificate is in Form 33` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the certificate sets out the nature of the default` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the reason for the default is known` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the certificate sets out the reason for the default` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the certificate sets out whether the ends of justice have been defeated or delayed by reason of the default` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the certificate sets out the names and addresses of the principal and sureties` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 770(1) the certificate is as the subsection requires` MEANS
    IF     `the certificate is in Form 33`
       AND `the certificate sets out the nature of the default`
       AND (`the certificate sets out the reason for the default` OR (NOT `the reason for the default is known`))
       AND `the certificate sets out whether the ends of justice have been defeated or delayed by reason of the default`
       AND `the certificate sets out the names and addresses of the principal and sureties`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "a certificate in Form 33 setting out (a) the nature of the default; (b) the reason for the default, if it is known; (c) ...; and (d) ..."

DECLARE `s 770(1) action` IS ONE OF
    `s 770(1) endorse or cause to be endorsed a certificate in Form 33 on the undertaking, release order or recognizance`

-- src:16579 | 770 (1) If, in proceedings to which this Act applies, a person who is subject to an undertaking, release order or recognizance does not comply with any of its conditions, a court, provincial court judge or justice having knowledge of the facts shall endorse or cause to be endorsed on the undertaking, release order or recognizance a certificate in Form 33 setting out
@ref s 770(1) (src:16579)
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 770(1) action`
`s 770(1) the duty of the court, provincial court judge or justice to endorse the certificate` MEANS
    PARTY `the court`
    MUST `s 770(1) endorse or cause to be endorsed a certificate in Form 33 on the undertaking, release order or recognizance`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY `the court` BECAUSE "the court did not endorse or cause to be endorsed a certificate on the undertaking, release order or recognizance"

-- (2) "Once endorsed, the undertaking, release order or recognizance must be sent to the clerk of the court and shall be kept by them with the records of the court."
-- The text does not say who sends it (fork F11); the function asks only whether it has been sent.
-- src:16585 | (2) Once endorsed, the undertaking, release order or recognizance must be sent to the clerk of the court and shall be kept by them with the records of the court.
@ref s 770(2) (src:16585)
GIVEN `the document has been endorsed` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the document has been sent to the clerk of the court` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 770(2) the document is sent to the clerk of the court as it must be` MEANS
    IF NOT `the document has been endorsed`
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Once endorsed, the undertaking, release order or recognizance must be sent to the clerk of the court"
    ELSE IF `the document has been sent to the clerk of the court`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "must be sent to the clerk of the court"

GIVEN `the document has been sent to the clerk of the court` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the clerk keeps the document with the records of the court` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 770(2) the clerk keeps the document with the records of the court as they shall` MEANS
    IF NOT `the document has been sent to the clerk of the court`
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Once endorsed, the undertaking, release order or recognizance must be sent to the clerk of the court and shall be kept by them"
    ELSE IF `the clerk keeps the document with the records of the court`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "shall be kept by them with the records of the court"

-- (3) "A certificate that has been endorsed on the undertaking, release order or recognizance is evidence of the default to which it relates."
-- src:16587 | (3) A certificate that has been endorsed on the undertaking, release order or recognizance is evidence of the default to which it relates.
@ref s 770(3) (src:16587)
GIVEN `the certificate has been endorsed on the undertaking, release order or recognizance` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 770(3) the certificate is evidence of the default to which it relates` MEANS
    IF `the certificate has been endorsed on the undertaking, release order or recognizance`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "A certificate that has been endorsed on the undertaking, release order or recognizance": the subsection speaks of that certificate, and is silent about any other

-- (4) "If, in proceedings to which this section applies, the principal or surety has deposited money as security for the performance of a condition of an undertaking, release order or recognizance, that money must be sent
-- to the clerk of the court with the defaulted undertaking, release order or recognizance, to be dealt with in accordance with this Part."
-- src:16589 | (4) If, in proceedings to which this section applies, the principal or surety has deposited money as security for the performance of a condition of an undertaking, release order or recognizance, that money must be sent to the clerk of the court with the defaulted undertaking, release order or recognizance, to be dealt with in accordance with this Part.
@ref s 770(4) (src:16589)
GIVEN `the principal or surety has deposited money as security for the performance of a condition of the document` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the money has been sent to the clerk of the court with the defaulted document` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 770(4) the money is sent to the clerk of the court with the defaulted document as it must be` MEANS
    IF NOT `the principal or surety has deposited money as security for the performance of a condition of the document`
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If, in proceedings to which this section applies, the principal or surety has deposited money as security for the performance of a condition of an undertaking, release order or recognizance"
    ELSE IF `the money has been sent to the clerk of the court with the defaulted document`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "that money must be sent to the clerk of the court with the defaulted undertaking, release order or recognizance"

§ `Part XXV, section 771: proceedings in case of default`

-- (1) "If an undertaking, release order or recognizance has been endorsed with a certificate and has been received by the clerk of the court, (a) a judge of the court shall, on the request of the clerk of the court or the
-- Attorney General or counsel acting on the Attorney General's or counsel's behalf, as the case may be, fix a time and place for the hearing of an application for the forfeiture of the amount set out in the undertaking,
-- release order or recognizance; and (b) the clerk of the court shall, not less than 10 days before the time fixed under paragraph (a) for the hearing, send by registered mail, or have served in the manner directed by the
-- court or prescribed by the rules of court, to each principal and surety, at the address set out in the certificate, a notice requiring the person to appear at the time and place fixed by the judge to show cause why the
-- amount set out in the undertaking, release order or recognizance should not be forfeited."
DECLARE `s 771(1)(a) requester` IS ONE OF
    `s 771(1)(a) the clerk of the court`
    `s 771(1)(a) the Attorney General`
    `s 771(1)(a) counsel acting on the Attorney General's or counsel's behalf`
    `s 771(1)(a) another person`

-- src:16591 | 771 (1) If an undertaking, release order or recognizance has been endorsed with a certificate and has been received by the clerk of the court,
-- src:16592 | (a) a judge of the court shall, on the request of the clerk of the court or the Attorney General or counsel acting on the Attorney General’s or counsel’s behalf, as the case may be, fix a time and place for the hearing of an application for the forfeiture of the amount set out in the undertaking, release order or recognizance; and
@ref s 771(1)(a) (src:16591-16592)
GIVEN `the document has been endorsed with a certificate and received by the clerk of the court` IS A BOOLEAN
      requester IS A `s 771(1)(a) requester`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 771(1)(a) a judge of the court shall fix a time and place for the hearing of an application for forfeiture` MEANS
    IF NOT `the document has been endorsed with a certificate and received by the clerk of the court`
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If an undertaking, release order or recognizance has been endorsed with a certificate and has been received by the clerk of the court"
    ELSE CONSIDER requester
         WHEN `s 771(1)(a) the clerk of the court` THEN JUST TRUE
         WHEN `s 771(1)(a) the Attorney General` THEN JUST TRUE
         WHEN `s 771(1)(a) counsel acting on the Attorney General's or counsel's behalf` THEN JUST TRUE
         WHEN `s 771(1)(a) another person` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "on the request of the clerk of the court or the Attorney General or counsel acting on the Attorney General's or counsel's behalf": the paragraph names who may request, and does not say that no one else may

-- src:16593 | (b) the clerk of the court shall, not less than 10 days before the time fixed under paragraph (a) for the hearing, send by registered mail, or have served in the manner directed by the court or prescribed by the rules of court, to each principal and surety, at the address set out in the certificate, a notice requiring the person to appear at the time and place fixed by the judge to show cause why the amount set out in the undertaking, release order or recognizance should not be forfeited.
@ref s 771(1)(b) (src:16593)
GIVEN `the number of days from the sending of the notice to the hearing` IS A NUMBER
      `the notice is sent by registered mail or served in the manner directed by the court or prescribed by the rules of court` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the notice is sent to each principal and surety at the address set out in the certificate` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the notice requires the person to appear at the time and place fixed by the judge to show cause why the amount should not be forfeited` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 771(1)(b) the clerk of the court sends the notice as the paragraph requires` MEANS
    IF     `the number of days from the sending of the notice to the hearing` AT LEAST 10
       AND `the notice is sent by registered mail or served in the manner directed by the court or prescribed by the rules of court`
       AND `the notice is sent to each principal and surety at the address set out in the certificate`
       AND `the notice requires the person to appear at the time and place fixed by the judge to show cause why the amount should not be forfeited`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "not less than 10 days before the time fixed under paragraph (a) for the hearing, send by registered mail, or have served in the manner directed by the court or prescribed by the rules of court, to each principal and surety, at the address set out in the certificate, a notice requiring the person to appear"

DECLARE `s 771(1)(b) action` IS ONE OF
    `s 771(1)(b) send or have served on each principal and surety a notice requiring the person to appear to show cause why the amount should not be forfeited`

-- src:16593 | (b) the clerk of the court shall, not less than 10 days before the time fixed under paragraph (a) for the hearing, send by registered mail, or have served in the manner directed by the court or prescribed by the rules of court, to each principal and surety, at the address set out in the certificate, a notice requiring the person to appear at the time and place fixed by the judge to show cause why the amount set out in the undertaking, release order or recognizance should not be forfeited.
@ref s 771(1)(b) (src:16593)
GIVEN `the number of days from today to the hearing` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 771(1)(b) action`
`s 771(1)(b) the clerk of the court's duty to send the notice` MEANS
    PARTY `the clerk of the court`
    MUST `s 771(1)(b) send or have served on each principal and surety a notice requiring the person to appear to show cause why the amount should not be forfeited`
    WITHIN `the number of days from today to the hearing` MINUS 10
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY `the clerk of the court` BECAUSE "the clerk of the court did not send the notice not less than 10 days before the hearing"

-- (2) "If subsection (1) has been complied with, the judge may, after giving the parties an opportunity to be heard, in the judge's discretion grant or refuse the application and make any order with respect to the
-- forfeiture of the amount that the judge considers proper."  A power ("may") with two gates: "after giving the parties an opportunity to be heard" (an "after" gate: JUST FALSE, listed in NOTES.md group (i));
-- "If subsection (1) has been complied with" (an "if" gate on a power: NOTHING, fork F3).
DECLARE `s 771(2) course` IS ONE OF
    `s 771(2) grant the application`
    `s 771(2) refuse the application`
    `s 771(2) make an order with respect to the forfeiture of the amount that the judge considers proper`
    `s 771(2) a course the subsection does not name`

-- src:16595 | (2) If subsection (1) has been complied with, the judge may, after giving the parties an opportunity to be heard, in the judge’s discretion grant or refuse the application and make any order with respect to the forfeiture of the amount that the judge considers proper.
@ref s 771(2) (src:16595)
GIVEN `subsection (1) has been complied with` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the judge has given the parties an opportunity to be heard` IS A BOOLEAN
      course IS A `s 771(2) course`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 771(2) the judge may take this course` MEANS
    IF NOT `the judge has given the parties an opportunity to be heard`
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "after giving the parties an opportunity to be heard"
    ELSE IF NOT `subsection (1) has been complied with`
         THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "If subsection (1) has been complied with, the judge may": a grant limited by an "if" gate; the subsection does not say the judge may not grant or refuse otherwise
         ELSE CONSIDER course
              WHEN `s 771(2) grant the application` THEN JUST TRUE
              WHEN `s 771(2) refuse the application` THEN JUST TRUE
              WHEN `s 771(2) make an order with respect to the forfeiture of the amount that the judge considers proper` THEN JUST TRUE
              WHEN `s 771(2) a course the subsection does not name` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): the courses are not closed with "only"

