      `the sheriff has executed the writ and dealt with the proceeds in the same manner as in civil proceedings in the province` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 772(1) the sheriff executes the writ and deals with the proceeds as the subsection requires` MEANS
    IF NOT `a writ of fieri facias is issued pursuant to section 771`
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where a writ of fieri facias is issued pursuant to section 771, the sheriff to whom it is delivered shall execute the writ"
    ELSE IF `the sheriff has executed the writ and dealt with the proceeds in the same manner as in civil proceedings in the province`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "shall execute the writ and deal with the proceeds thereof in the same manner"

DECLARE `s 772(1) action` IS ONE OF
    `s 772(1) execute the writ and deal with the proceeds in the same manner as in civil proceedings in the province`

