    `s 772(2) the tariff applicable in the superior court of the province in civil proceedings (any other province)`

-- src:16605 | (2) Where this section applies, the Crown is entitled to the costs of execution and of proceedings incidental thereto that are fixed, in the Province of Quebec, by any tariff applicable in the Superior Court in civil proceedings, and in any other province, by any tariff applicable in the superior court of the province in civil proceedings, as the judge may direct.
@ref s 772(2) (src:16605)
GIVEN place IS A `Province or territory`
GIVETH A MAYBE `s 772(2) tariff`
`s 772(2) the tariff that fixes the costs` MEANS
    CONSIDER place
    WHEN Quebec THEN JUST `s 772(2) the tariff applicable in the Superior Court in civil proceedings (the Province of Quebec)`
    WHEN Ontario THEN JUST `s 772(2) the tariff applicable in the superior court of the province in civil proceedings (any other province)`
    WHEN `Nova Scotia` THEN JUST `s 772(2) the tariff applicable in the superior court of the province in civil proceedings (any other province)`
    WHEN `British Columbia` THEN JUST `s 772(2) the tariff applicable in the superior court of the province in civil proceedings (any other province)`
    WHEN `Prince Edward Island` THEN JUST `s 772(2) the tariff applicable in the superior court of the province in civil proceedings (any other province)`
    WHEN `Newfoundland and Labrador` THEN JUST `s 772(2) the tariff applicable in the superior court of the province in civil proceedings (any other province)`
    WHEN `New Brunswick` THEN JUST `s 772(2) the tariff applicable in the superior court of the province in civil proceedings (any other province)`
    WHEN Manitoba THEN JUST `s 772(2) the tariff applicable in the superior court of the province in civil proceedings (any other province)`
    WHEN Saskatchewan THEN JUST `s 772(2) the tariff applicable in the superior court of the province in civil proceedings (any other province)`
    WHEN Alberta THEN JUST `s 772(2) the tariff applicable in the superior court of the province in civil proceedings (any other province)`
    WHEN Yukon THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "in the Province of Quebec ... and in any other province": a territory is not a province, and the subsection names no tariff for it
    WHEN `Northwest Territories` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "in any other province": a territory is not a province
    WHEN Nunavut THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "in any other province": a territory is not a province

§ `Part XXV, section 773: committal when a writ is not satisfied`

-- (1) "Where a writ of fieri facias has been issued under this Part and it appears from a certificate in a return made by the sheriff that sufficient goods and chattels, lands and tenements cannot be found to satisfy
-- the writ, or that the proceeds of the execution of the writ are not sufficient to satisfy it, a judge of the court may, upon the application of the Attorney General or counsel acting on his behalf, fix a time and
-- place for the sureties to show cause why a warrant of committal should not be issued in respect of them."  A power ("may") with "where" and "upon" gates (JUST FALSE, listed in NOTES.md group (i)).
-- src:16607 | 773 (1) Where a writ of fieri facias has been issued under this Part and it appears from a certificate in a return made by the sheriff that sufficient goods and chattels, lands and tenements cannot be found to satisfy the writ, or that the proceeds of the execution of the writ are not sufficient to satisfy it, a judge of the court may, upon the application of the Attorney General or counsel acting on his behalf, fix a time and place for the sureties to show cause why a warrant of committal should not be issued in respect of them.
@ref s 773(1) (src:16607)
GIVEN `a writ of fieri facias has been issued under this Part` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it appears from a certificate in a return made by the sheriff that sufficient goods and chattels, lands and tenements cannot be found to satisfy the writ` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it appears from the certificate that the proceeds of the execution of the writ are not sufficient to satisfy it` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the application is made by the Attorney General or counsel acting on the Attorney General's behalf` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 773(1) a judge of the court may fix a time and place for the sureties to show cause` MEANS
    IF NOT (`a writ of fieri facias has been issued under this Part` AND (`it appears from a certificate in a return made by the sheriff that sufficient goods and chattels, lands and tenements cannot be found to satisfy the writ` OR `it appears from the certificate that the proceeds of the execution of the writ are not sufficient to satisfy it`))
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where a writ of fieri facias has been issued under this Part and it appears from a certificate in a return made by the sheriff that sufficient goods and chattels, lands and tenements cannot be found to satisfy the writ, or that the proceeds of the execution of the writ are not sufficient to satisfy it"
    ELSE IF `the application is made by the Attorney General or counsel acting on the Attorney General's behalf`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "upon the application of the Attorney General or counsel acting on his behalf"

-- (2) "Seven clear days notice of the time and place fixed for the hearing pursuant to subsection (1) shall be given to the sureties."  Clear days leave out the day the notice is given and the day of the hearing: the
-- number of clear days is the difference of the two days less one. The text does not say who gives the notice (fork F11).
-- src:16609 | (2) Seven clear days notice of the time and place fixed for the hearing pursuant to subsection (1) shall be given to the sureties.
@ref s 773(2) (src:16609)
GIVEN `the date the notice is given` IS A DATE
      `the date of the hearing` IS A DATE
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 773(2) the number of clear days of notice` MEANS (Day `the date of the hearing` MINUS Day `the date the notice is given`) MINUS 1

@ref s 773(2) (src:16609)
GIVEN `the date the notice is given` IS A DATE
      `the date of the hearing` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 773(2) the notice given to the sureties is seven clear days notice` MEANS
    IF `s 773(2) the number of clear days of notice` `the date the notice is given` `the date of the hearing` AT LEAST 7
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Seven clear days notice of the time and place fixed for the hearing pursuant to subsection (1) shall be given to the sureties"

-- (3) "The judge shall, at the hearing held pursuant to subsection (1), inquire into the circumstances of the case and may in his discretion (a) order the discharge of the amount for which the surety is liable; or
-- (b) make any order with respect to the surety and to his imprisonment that he considers proper in the circumstances and issue a warrant of committal in Form 27."
