    IF NOT `the hearing is held pursuant to subsection (1)`
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The judge shall, at the hearing held pursuant to subsection (1), inquire into the circumstances of the case"
    ELSE IF `the judge inquires into the circumstances of the case`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "shall, at the hearing ..., inquire into the circumstances of the case"

DECLARE `s 773(3) order` IS ONE OF
    `s 773(3)(a) order the discharge of the amount for which the surety is liable`
    `s 773(3)(b) make an order with respect to the surety and to the surety's imprisonment that the judge considers proper and issue a warrant of committal in Form 27`
