         ELSE CONSIDER prison
              WHEN `s 773(4) a prison in the territorial division in which the writ was issued` THEN JUST TRUE
              WHEN `s 773(4) the prison nearest to the court` THEN JUST TRUE
              WHEN `s 773(4) another prison` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the subsection names the prisons, and does not say that no other prison will do

-- (5) "In this section and in section 771, Attorney General means, where subsection 734.4(2) applies, the Attorney General of Canada."  A "means" definition under a "where": the person is the Attorney General of Canada
-- where 734.4(2) applies. Whether 734.4(2) applies is the answer of another part (taken as an input).
-- src:16617 | (5) In this section and in section 771, Attorney General means, where subsection 734.4(2) applies, the Attorney General of Canada.
@ref s 773(5) "Attorney General" (src:16617)
GIVEN `subsection 734.4(2) applies, by s 734.4(2)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the person is the Attorney General of Canada` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 773(5) the person is the Attorney General for the purposes of section 771 and this section` MEANS
    CONSIDER `subsection 734.4(2) applies, by s 734.4(2)`
    WHEN JUST TRUE THEN
        IF `the person is the Attorney General of Canada`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Attorney General means, where subsection 734.4(2) applies, the Attorney General of Canada"
    WHEN JUST FALSE THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): where subsection 734.4(2) does not apply, this subsection gives no meaning; the meaning is that of section 2
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): the answer of s 734.4(2) is itself not covered
